<title>SLOVAKIA: Details of Slovak February consumer inflation.</title>
<headline>Details of Slovak February consumer inflation.</headline>
<dateline>BRATISLAVA 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following are details of February Slovak consumer inflation, as released by the Statistical Bureau (SUSR) on Tuesday.</p>
<p> SLOVAK CONSUMER INFLATION     Feb 97     Jan 97   Feb 96</p>
<p>  pct change mo/mo		  0.4	   1.1	0.3</p>
<p>  pct change yr/yr		  6.0	   5.8	n/a</p>
<p>Foodstuffs, soft drinks</p>
<p>  pct change month/month	  0.4	   1.7     -0.7</p>
<p>  pct change year/year	    6.6	   5.4	n/a</p>
<p>Leisure and culture</p>
<p> pct change month/month	   0.5	   1.4	0.6</p>
<p>  pct change year/year	    3.9	   4.1	n/a</p>
<p>Hotels, cafes, restaurants</p>
<p>  pct change month/month	  0.2	   1.3	0.8</p>
<p>  pct change year/year	    7.0	   7.7	n/a</p>
<p>Transportation</p>
<p>  pct change month/month	  0.3	   1.0	0.4</p>
<p>  pct change year/year	    6.7	   6.9	n/a</p>
<p>Household, energy, utilities and fuels</p>
<p>  pct change month/month	  0.4	   0.6	0.8</p>
<p>  pct change year/year	    5.0	   5.4	n/a</p>
<p>Alcohol, tobacco and pharmaceuticals</p>
<p>  pct change month/month	  0.4	   0.8	0.4</p>
<p>  pct change year/year	    4.4	   4.2	n/a</p>
<p>Furniture, household appliances and maintenance</p>
<p>  pct change month/month	  0.5	   0.3	0.4</p>
<p>  pct change year/year	    4.5	   4.3	n/a</p>
<p>Education</p>
<p>  pct change month/month	  0.2	   0.9	0.3</p>
<p>  pct change year/year	   12.4	  12.5	n/a</p>
<p>Healthcare</p>
<p>  pct change month/month	  0.8	   0.4	2.7</p>
<p>  pct change year/year	    9.0	  11.1	n/a</p>
<p>Clothes and shoes</p>
<p>  pct change month/month	  0.5	   0.6	0.4</p>
<p>  pct change year/year	    7.4	   7.2	n/a</p>
<p>Various goods and services</p>
<p>  pct change month/month	  0.8	   0.7	0.4</p>
<p>  pct change year/year	    4.8	   4.4	n/a</p>
<p>Note: SUSR said that due to the changes in the population's expenditure structure, it had revised formulas for calcuating CPI, using 1995 as a base year. SUSR did not release revised figures for 1996 under the new formula.</p>
<p>-- Bratislava Newsroom, 42-7-521-8402</p>
